(5502436, 792741, 104955, '<td valign="top">Not my fav color, but definitely my blue ribbon fav pic. From the dark contrast of the sky, to the gentle breeze in the trees, to the "whale of a light" and its reflection, it is just magic. The lighting on the car is purrfect.</td>', 'Not my fav color, but definitely my blue ribbon fav pic. From the dark contrast of the sky, to the gentle breeze in the trees, to the "whale of a light" and its reflection, it is just magic. The lighting on the car is purrfect.', '2009-05-27 15:13:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(5502494, 793329, 106848, '<td valign="top">Great detail, <br/>shadowing and lighting.<br/> <br/>10/10</td>', 'Great detail, shadowing and lighting. 10/10', '2009-05-27 15:39:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(5502501, 793376, 67237, '<td valign="top">The main subject and the background are interesting enough to achieve a good ad image. I would give this a 5 though, because (IMO) a few technical and concept issues have ruined that object:<br/>1.- The worst mistake is conceptual: the use of a kind of "motivational poster" design with fonts, color and a slogan that this famous brand (or any other brand)would never use. <br/>2.- On the processing: you could have (and should have) used the advanced editing rules to solve these issues:<br/>a)compensate the (under) exposure of most of the car...and maybe get some very subtle detail on that tree. Dim a little the excess of light on the grass.<br/>b) clone out those two distracting whitish things on the grass: one in front of the car, the other one below the rear wheel, close to the lower edege of the image.<br/>3.- On the shooting: you could have solved part of the issues mentioned above by moving the car 2 or 3 feet closer to the camera position.</td>', 'The main subject and the background are interesting enough to achieve a good ad image. I would give this a 5 though, because (IMO) a few technical and concept issues have ruined that object:1.- The worst mistake is conceptual: the use of a kind of "motivational poster" design with fonts, color and a slogan that this famous brand (or any other brand)would never use. 2.- On the processing: you could have (and should have) used the advanced editing rules to solve these issues:a)compensate the (under) exposure of most of the car...and maybe get some very subtle detail on that tree. Dim a little the excess of light on the grass.b) clone out those two distracting whitish things on the grass: one in front of the car, the other one below the rear wheel, close to the lower edege of the image.3.- On the shooting: you could have solved part of the issues mentioned above by moving the car 2 or 3 feet closer to the camera position.', '2009-05-27 15:46:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5502512, 792087, 67237, '<td valign="top">Is SO MUCH blurring legal?. Other than that a good composition, color control and graphic design. <br/>A left hand drive with a London plate? :-) It must be another London somewhere.</td>', 'Is SO MUCH blurring legal?. Other than that a good composition, color control and graphic design. A left hand drive with a London plate? :-) It must be another London somewhere.', '2009-05-27 15:55:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5502513, 793082, 63812, '<td valign="top">excellent image. you deserve a ribbon..i vote 10</td>', 'excellent image. you deserve a ribbon..i vote 10', '2009-05-27 15:56:43.000000', NULL, 1),
