(5507869, 793426, 67152, '<td valign="top">Andres - That first outtake would have taken the Blue....thanks for entering the one you did ;-)<br/> <br/>Congrats on all your images posted - you are the master of this type of shot and I am happy to be in the same area as your shot.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-06-01 06:15:59.</i></td>', 'Andres - That first outtake would have taken the Blue....thanks for entering the one you did ;-) Congrats on all your images posted - you are the master of this type of shot and I am happy to be in the same area as your shot.', '2009-06-01 07:14:55.000000', '2009-06-01 07:15:59.000000', 0),
(5507871, 792374, 103032, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mpeters:</b></div><hr/><i> Is this the famous Oregon beach wreck? Had no idea it was so large, or is it? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I just Googled it, yes it''s the shipwreck near Astoria, OR.  (I live in Oregon, I just learned something today...)</td>', 'Originally posted by mpeters: Is this the famous Oregon beach wreck? Had no idea it was so large, or is it?   I just Googled it, yes it''s the shipwreck near Astoria, OR.  (I live in Oregon, I just learned something today...)', '2009-06-01 07:21:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5507885, 792374, 60173, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by lky623:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mpeters:</b></div><hr/><i> Is this the famous Oregon beach wreck? Had no idea it was so large, or is it? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I just Googled it, yes it''s the shipwreck near Astoria, OR.  (I live in Oregon, I just learned something today...) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>There''s apparently several shipwrecks in the area, but this one is by far the easiest to get to. It''s just a quick 2 minute trek through the sand from the parking lot.<br/> <br/>As for the slogan used, I''m not sure where the cars were gaining access to the beach, but "just because they can, doesn''t mean they should!" I couldn''t believe that there were cars driving that close to such a fragile historical landmark. There''s parts of the wreckage that are just barely poking through the sand. Dangerous for both the drivers and the wreckage.</td>', 'Originally posted by lky623: Originally posted by mpeters: Is this the famous Oregon beach wreck? Had no idea it was so large, or is it?   I just Googled it, yes it''s the shipwreck near Astoria, OR.  (I live in Oregon, I just learned something today...)   There''s apparently several shipwrecks in the area, but this one is by far the easiest to get to. It''s just a quick 2 minute trek through the sand from the parking lot. As for the slogan used, I''m not sure where the cars were gaining access to the beach, but "just because they can, doesn''t mean they should!" I couldn''t believe that there were cars driving that close to such a fragile historical landmark. There''s parts of the wreckage that are just barely poking through the sand. Dangerous for both the drivers and the wreckage.', '2009-06-01 07:43:30.000000', NULL, 0),
