(5508666, 793082, 85927, '<td valign="top">Wonderful image, but the caption gives it all its punch and strength.<br/> <br/>Some people mistook the name of the challenge for "Picture of a car" instead of "automobile ad".  You really added a great sales pitch: respect!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Wonderful image, but the caption gives it all its punch and strength. Some people mistook the name of the challenge for "Picture of a car" instead of "automobile ad".  You really added a great sales pitch: respect! ', '2009-06-01 17:00:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5508761, 792087, 67237, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> Pretty slick. The glow is so over the top but it definitely helps to make this one stand out from the pack. Since this was advance editing the clipped highlights should have been fixed and I think you missed a spot when blurring the background (i.e. near the bumper). Other than that very professional. Congrats. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I did not vote on this challenge (just commented on a couple of images and this was one of them). It sure looks like an ad, and it''s so good at it that the issues pointed out by Yanko do not detract..and that tells a lot about the excellence of the overall work.. so huge congrats on the entry, the ribbon and the new PB!!! <br/> <br/>In regards to "you missed a spot when blurring the background (i.e. near the bumper)". It brings up a doubt I have always had in regards to the extent of "legal" blurring.<br/> <br/>The rule says the blur filter can be applied as long as it doesn´t change the way a viewer would have described the original image. Would it be legal to use bluring to get rid of some people and cars or buildings on the background, or the activity inside the building?. Could someone clarify please?<br/> <br/>(edited for spelling)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-06-01 18:50:11.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by yanko: Pretty slick. The glow is so over the top but it definitely helps to make this one stand out from the pack. Since this was advance editing the clipped highlights should have been fixed and I think you missed a spot when blurring the background (i.e. near the bumper). Other than that very professional. Congrats.   I did not vote on this challenge (just commented on a couple of images and this was one of them). It sure looks like an ad, and it''s so good at it that the issues pointed out by Yanko do not detract..and that tells a lot about the excellence of the overall work.. so huge congrats on the entry, the ribbon and the new PB!!!  In regards to "you missed a spot when blurring the background (i.e. near the bumper)". It brings up a doubt I have always had in regards to the extent of "legal" blurring. The rule says the blur filter can be applied as long as it doesn´t change the way a viewer would have described the original image. Would it be legal to use bluring to get rid of some people and cars or buildings on the background, or the activity inside the building?. Could someone clarify please? (edited for spelling)', '2009-06-01 18:21:07.000000', '2009-06-01 19:50:11.000000', 0),
(5508768, 792087, 52500, '<td valign="top">Great job indeed.  Any way you could post the original for us?  I''m also wondering about the legality of blurring and how much might be ok.</td>', 'Great job indeed.  Any way you could post the original for us?  I''m also wondering about the legality of blurring and how much might be ok.', '2009-06-01 18:35:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5508786, 792513, 63503, '<td valign="top">Peter, congratulations on a great image and most deserved blue ribbon !!</td>', 'Peter, congratulations on a great image and most deserved blue ribbon !!', '2009-06-01 18:51:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5508869, 793314, 72134, '<td valign="top">On our way home, where we looked at some nice waterfalls, it started raining and the sun was trying to shine trough rainbows apearded. We had to cross some small rivers and after crossing one of them I thought "I want some ad for automobile" we changed seats and my wife went bak over the river and took place on the other side and took the shoots, we did it three times on different speed of the truck, it was a bit difficult because there waa som large rocks on the bottom of the ford, but it was OK, this is a strong truck on 35" tiers. And I used the front lights and dumper in the text Hilux: Maybe it was a mistake, but to me it seemed cool, but it probably takes to much attention from the rest of the picture.<br/>Great thanks for the comments, this was the highest rated I''ve got in this DP.</td>', 'On our way home, where we looked at some nice waterfalls, it started raining and the sun was trying to shine trough rainbows apearded. We had to cross some small rivers and after crossing one of them I thought "I want some ad for automobile" we changed seats and my wife went bak over the river and took place on the other side and took the shoots, we did it three times on different speed of the truck, it was a bit difficult because there waa som large rocks on the bottom of the ford, but it was OK, this is a strong truck on 35" tiers. And I used the front lights and dumper in the text Hilux: Maybe it was a mistake, but to me it seemed cool, but it probably takes to much attention from the rest of the picture.Great thanks for the comments, this was the highest rated I''ve got in this DP.', '2009-06-01 20:10:02.000000', NULL, 0),
